# Gitignored paths that `wt step copy-ignored` clones into a new worktree.
# A file must be BOTH gitignored and matched here to be copied.
#
# These are reflink copies on APFS/btrfs: blocks are shared with the primary
# worktree until something rewrites them, so a 14 GB tree costs seconds and
# almost no disk. Cold-starting them instead means a full Rust build plus two
# npm installs plus a ~300 MB VS Code download in every worktree.

# Rust build artifacts. The single biggest cold-start cost in this repo.
target/

# Node dependencies for the two companion packages.
.obsidian/plugins/criv/node_modules/
extensions/vscode-criv/node_modules/

# Downloaded VS Code builds used by the extension integration test.
extensions/vscode-criv/.vscode-test/

# Deliberately NOT copied:
#   .criv/        generated vault state; rebuilt per worktree by `criv watch --once`
#   *.vsix        packaging output, cheap to regenerate
#   PLAN.md       local scratch planning files
